g voters that they had lost control over their lives. Crosby argued that th=
is sense of lost control was stoking subversive political movements and par=
ties across democracies in the west. He also warned that those groups would=
 eventually be judged on whether they could deliver improvements rather tha=
n simply challenge the government.&nbsp;</span>
</p><p dir=3D"ltr" style=3D"margin:0;font-size:18px;mso-line-height-alt:21p=
